    3. For each distractor, build an open shape (polyomino that does not enclose a 4-connected hole); e.g. random-walk or L/U/C shape
    4. Place all objects on the grid with Chebyshev separation >= 3 between any rim and any other object (>= 2 between distractors); rim objects may overlap the grid edge
    5. Verify no spurious holes exist (all black components except the intended holes are edge-connected)
